1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,642
Welcome to Atomic Education.

2
00:00:02,701 --> 00:00:09,796
This lesson was written by the Atomic teaching team to help you learn Cambridge Lower Secondary Science with confidence.

3
00:00:09,796 --> 00:00:10,500
Let's begin!

4
00:00:11,558 --> 00:00:13,787
Welcome to Unit 14: Planetary Systems.

5
00:00:14,845 --> 00:00:18,774
The Universe is everything: all of space, time, matter and energy.

6
00:00:18,774 --> 00:00:24,228
Looking at the night sky, you see cosmic history, because starlight takes years to reach us.

7
00:00:24,228 --> 00:00:26,574
But light pollution is hiding the stars.

8
00:00:27,632 --> 00:00:31,561
On a truly dark night, you can see the Milky Way, our home galaxy.

9
00:00:31,561 --> 00:00:37,191
It's a spiral galaxy, like a giant spinning pinwheel, containing hundreds of billions of stars.

10
00:00:37,191 --> 00:00:42,117
Our Sun is on one of its spiral arms, about 27 thousand light years from the centre.

11
00:00:43,175 --> 00:00:45,931
The Milky Way is one of trillions of galaxies.

12
00:00:45,931 --> 00:00:52,030
It belongs to a Local Group of about 54 galaxies held together by gravity. Our closest major neighbour,

13
00:00:52,030 --> 00:00:56,897
Andromeda, is heading our way, but it will take about four billion years to arrive!

14
00:00:57,956 --> 00:01:02,178
Galaxies come in different shapes. Spiral galaxies like ours have arms.

15
00:01:02,178 --> 00:01:04,993
Elliptical galaxies are oval, like rugby balls.

16
00:01:04,993 --> 00:01:11,150
Lenticular galaxies are lens-shaped with a bulge in the middle. Irregular galaxies have no defined shape.

17
00:01:12,209 --> 00:01:18,307
A galaxy contains stars, planetary systems, gas and clouds of stellar dust: tiny specks of ice, carbon,

18
00:01:18,307 --> 00:01:22,471
silicon, oxygen and metals. Unlike house dust, it isn't skin and hair!

19
00:01:22,471 --> 00:01:26,752
It blocks our view, but it's the building block of new planetary systems.

20
00:01:27,810 --> 00:01:29,687
The Universe is also expanding.

21
00:01:29,687 --> 00:01:35,199
Imagine galaxies as dots on a balloon being blown up: they all move further and further apart.

22
00:01:36,258 --> 00:01:41,242
Six dots are drawn on a balloon to stand for galaxies. Then the balloon is blown up.

23
00:01:41,242 --> 00:01:45,816
Predict: what will happen to the distances between the dots? Pause and decide.

24
00:01:46,875 --> 00:01:50,628
Watch. As the balloon is blown up, the dots start to move apart.

25
00:01:51,686 --> 00:01:57,961
When the balloon is fully blown up, every dot is further from every other dot, and no dot is at the centre.

26
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:04,004
Explain what you saw. The dots move apart because the rubber between them stretches.

27
00:02:04,004 --> 00:02:10,455
In the same way, space itself is stretching, so distant galaxies are moving away from us and from each other.

28
00:02:10,455 --> 00:02:15,615
This is evidence that the Universe is expanding. Pause and explain it in your own words.
